course: dictionary
lesson: 6805
title: Words ending in -er
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you who does something or what does something. The ending -er often shows this. An organiser is a person who organises, which means planning and arranging things. Organisers plan events like a party, a trip or a sports day.
explain: Look at the words around the word to check its meaning. «A pill organiser with the days of the week helps people who take several medicines take the right ones at the right time.» The words pill and days of the week tell you an organiser can also be a thing, not a person. It is a box that keeps things in order.
explain: Now try the swap test. Put your meaning in place of the word and read the sentence again. A desk organiser is a tray or box that keeps pens and paper tidy on your desk. If the sentence still makes sense with your meaning, you have probably got it right.
fact: An organiser is a person who plans and arranges an event or activity.
fact: An organiser can also be a box, folder, diary or app that helps you keep things in order.
fact: «A pill organiser with the days of the week» helps people take their medicines at the right time.
fact: «A desk organiser» and «a personal organiser» are things you use to keep your work and time in order.
fact: In American English the spelling is organizer, with a z, but the meaning is the same.
exercise: «A pill organiser with the days of the week helps people take the right medicines at the right time.» What is a pill organiser? | A machine that makes medicine | A kind of bottle for water | *A box with the days of the week that keeps pills in order | A doctor who writes prescriptions
exercise: Mia is the organiser of the class party. What does organiser mean here? | A kind of cake | A box that holds party hats | *A person who plans and arranges the party | A guest who arrives late
exercise: Which of these is a personal organiser? | A sports coach who trains a team | A tall tree in the park | A pencil case with wheels | *A diary or planner that helps you keep your time in order
test: Ben is planning the sports day for the whole school. What does that make him? | A referee who blows the whistle | A prize for the best team | A medal winner | *A person who plans and arranges the event
test: Which of these is a desk organiser? | A chair with wheels | *A tray or box that keeps pens and paper tidy | A rug for the floor | A lamp that glows in the dark
exam: Read this: «The trip organiser checked the bus times.» What does organiser mean? | A bus driver | A map of the town | *A person who plans and arranges the trip | A ticket for the bus
